{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>If the anointed priest sins to the guilt of the people.</b> Its midrash: he is liable only for הֶעְלֵם דָּבָר together with inadvertent deed, as it says ״לְאַשְׁמַת הָעָם וְנֶעְלַם דָּבָר מֵעֵינֵי הַקָּהָל וְעָשׂוּ״ (ibid.); and its plain sense according to aggadah: when a high priest sins — this is the guilt of the people, for they depend on him to make atonement for them and to pray on their behalf, and he has become flawed." "<b>A bull.</b> One might say an old one — Scripture says ״בֶּן״ (son). If ״בֶּן,״ one might say a young one — Scripture says ״פַּר״ (bull). How so? This is a bull in its third year (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:56.788342911Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}